                <pb facs="0588" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/943: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cottrell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-31T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>10. Your May 24th, noon.</p>
                <p>You will inform the Government of Bolivia that the question of Bolivia’s
                    participation in the discussions which are now being carried on between Chile
                    and Peru, and which relate to questions arising out of a treaty of which these
                    two countries were the only signatories, is a matter for the exclusive
                    consideration of the two countries <pb facs="0589" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>
                    concerned, and the Government of the United States regrets that it feels unable
                    to take any initiative in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
